EXERCISED PATH: model/layers.py:169-183 plus model/frechet_poincare.py:56-99 and model/model.py:87-94 | Exercised by reading the autograd graph and the switch branches (no PyTorch in this sandbox): quant_loss = beta*(weights*commitment).mean() + mse(x, x_q.detach()) has two live gradient terms; commitment = poincare_distance(point, codebook[embed_ind].detach())**2 depends on point = clamp_ball(exp_0(latent)) and therefore reaches the encoder MLP; the straight-through x_q = x + (x_q - x).detach() (layers.py:182) carries the recon gradient; the codebook is deliberately requires_grad=False (layers.py:78-84) because its only estimator is the detached Frechet step, so no gradient claim is dead. Every map clamps (mobius denominator 1e-12 at 39, atanh argument 1-1e-7 at 77/84/97, ball radius 1-1e-4 at 42-53), so the worst case is a saturated zero derivative rather than inf/nan, and apply() keeps the old slot when the move is non-finite (197-199). use_behaviour=False zeroes the weighting of both the commitment and the slot mean; use_curvature=False swaps cost, tangent and step to the Euclidean branches while the weights stay; both flags are read from USE_BEHAVIOUR/USE_GEOMETRY (train_rqvae.py:101-102, 250-251) and threaded into every level (layers.py:320-324). Two non-blocking deviations are reported below.

FINDING SEVERITY: minor
FINDING LOCATION: model/layers.py:198-200
FINDING DETAIL: init_codebook computes the level-1..3 start assignment with self.frechet.distances(x, codebook) where x is the raw encoder latent, not the ball point used in training (layers.py:153). poincare_distance/mobius_add assume both arguments lie in the unit ball (frechet_poincare.py:26-39, 88-98); for ||x|| >= 1 the Mobius denominator is clamped at 1e-12 and every distance saturates at the atanh clamp, so the argmin degenerates and the residual that initialises the next level's KMeans is built from one arbitrary slot. The docstring at layers.py:196-197 claims this is the "same cost and same residual as the training step", which it is not.
FINDING REPRODUCTION: build VQLayer(256, 32, frechet=True, use_curvature=True), call init_codebook on latents with row norm > 1 (e.g. 2.0*randn(1024,32)), and compare the returned residual with the residual of the training path point = clamp_ball(exp_0(x)); for out-of-ball rows every entry of the cost matrix is the same saturated value.
FINDING CORRECTION: use the training point in the init assignment and residual, i.e. clamp_ball(exp_0(x)) as in layers.py:153.

FINDING SEVERITY: minor
FINDING LOCATION: model/layers.py:347
FINDING DETAIL: the residual handed to level l+1 is x - log_0(c_{a(i)}), a difference of tangent images, whereas the specification defines r_i = log^kappa_{c_{l,a(i)}}(z_i). They agree only to first order near the origin, so the level-2/3 assignment geometry differs from the stated mechanism.
FINDING REPRODUCTION: read layers.py:344-348 with frechet_poincare.py:73-85; with a slot at radius 0.99 and a point on the opposite side, log_0(point) - log_0(slot) and log_at(slot, point) differ by an unbounded factor.
FINDING CORRECTION: subtract through the logarithmic map at the chosen slot (log_at(codebook[embed_ind], point)) instead of the two log_0 images.

